# Frontend Apps

## Site (`apps/site`)

Unified Next.js app for customer ordering and staff dashboards. Runs on port 3000.

### Customer

- Mobile-first; no authentication
- Entry: `/store/{storeId}/table/{tableId}`
- Flow: load store → menu → cart → checkout → order tracking
- Persist cart in localStorage; associate orders with table from URL

### Staff

Staff routes use a path segment: `/{path}/kitchen` and `/{path}/admin`.

- `path` defaults to `NEXT_PUBLIC_STAFF_PATH`, then `NEXT_PUBLIC_KITCHEN_STORE_ID`, then `"staff"`
- Use `PathProvider` / `usePathContext()` / `useIsAdmin()` to detect admin vs kitchen vs customer routes

- `/{path}/kitchen` — Desktop-first KDS with four status columns; real-time via Socket.IO
- `/{path}/admin` — Desktop-first store management; JWT auth required (MANAGER+)
- Audio alert on `order.created`; support full-screen mode on kitchen view

## Conventions

- Next.js App Router, TypeScript strict, TailwindCSS + shadcn/ui
- Server Components for data fetching; Client Components for interactivity and sockets
- Shared types in a `packages/types` or `packages/shared` workspace package
